From: ArchPad project <archpad@localhost>
Subject: media: i2c: hi846: allow sensor power-up to settle

The HI846 on pipa intermittently fails its initial I2C ID read despite a
correct reset pulse.  Vendor-era HI846 bring-up used a substantially longer
settling interval than the upstream driver's 30-60 microseconds.  Wait 100 ms
after reset release before accessing registers.  This is a probe-only delay
and does not change the streaming sequence.

---
 drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
index 3a7ef4d36f25..a3693b98f8f1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
@@ -1825,7 +1825,7 @@ static int hi846_power_on(struct hi846 *hi846)
 	usleep_range(30, 60);
 	if (hi846->rst_gpio)
 		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(hi846->rst_gpio, 0);
-	usleep_range(30, 60);
+	msleep(100);
 
 	return 0;
 
